      "message": "with the same semantics (`(old,new) in _LEGAL_TRANSITIONS`), **no import of `semkg_contract`**.\n- `consume(old, new)` \u2014 returns `(allowed, reason)`: `(True,\"ok\")` for the two legal v1 edges; `(False,\"missing_state\")` if either side is `None`; otherwise `(False,\"illegal_transition\")`. Unknown states such as `paid -> new`, `new -> shipped`, or `new -> new` are denied, exactly as contract v1 would deny them.\n\n**`attempts/B_transitive_attempt_1/_check.py`** (throwaway local check)\n- Exercises legal, illegal, and missing-state cases; output was `[(True,'ok'), (True,'ok'), (False,'illegal_transition'), (False,'illegal_transition'), (False,'missing_state'), (False,'illegal_transition')]` and `CONTRACT_VERSION 1`, so all assertions pass.\n\nNote on paths: writes with relative paths resolved under `attempts/B_transitive_attempt_1/`, not the repo root (my first check invocation failed for that reason); no files outside that directory were created or modified, and no repository-wide tests were run."
